cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it as below."
title: "factorio-evolution: natural selection among self-copying machines in vanilla Factorio"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "hjkornn-phys"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hjkornn-phys/factorio-evolution"
abstract: >-
  A colony of self-copying machines in vanilla Factorio 2.1 in which a
  cheaper lineage outgrows a costlier one by natural selection; the only
  scripted act is placing a machine's blueprint where it asks, and plates
  and power are supplied. Light's share 0.587 against 0.380 in a
  cost-free control, 10 runs an arm, exact p = 5.4e-6.
keywords:
  - factorio
  - artificial-life
  - self-replication
  - evolution
  - circuit-network
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-09-30
